**Answer**

Leaving out patches and tests, `erpnext/stock/stock_balance.py::update_bin_qty` has seven callers. Six of them pass only some of the four keys, so they would start raising. One passes all four and would keep working.

**Callers that would fail (they pass partial dicts):**

1. `erpnext/selling/doctype/sales_order/services/reservation.py::SalesOrderStockReservation.update_reserved_qty` passes only `reserved_qty`. It is reached through `SalesOrder.update_reserved_qty` when you:
   - submit or cancel a Sales Order (`SalesOrder.on_submit` / `on_cancel`);
   - close, reopen or hold one, or close one of its items (`selling/.../services/status.py::StatusService.update_status` / `recalculate_after_item_close`);
   - "Update Items" on a submitted Sales Order (`accounts/services/child_item_update.py::ChildItemUpdater._post_update`);
   - submit or cancel a Delivery Note or Sales Invoice linked to a Sales Order (`controllers/selling_controller.py`, line 620).
2. `erpnext/buying/doctype/purchase_order/purchase_order.py::PurchaseOrder.update_ordered_qty` passes only `ordered_qty`. Triggers: submitting or cancelling a Purchase Order, closing or reopening one (`buying/.../services/status.py`), and "Update Items" on a submitted Purchase Order.
3. `erpnext/stock/doctype/material_request/material_request.py::MaterialRequest.update_requested_qty` passes only `indented_qty`. Triggers:
   - submitting, cancelling or stopping a Material Request;
   - Purchase Order submit, cancel or "Update Items";
   - Subcontracting Order status changes;
   - Stock Entry and Work Order flows that call it on linked Material Requests.
4. `erpnext/subcontracting/doctype/subcontracting_order/subcontracting_order.py::SubcontractingOrder.update_ordered_qty_for_subcontracting` passes only `ordered_qty`. It is reached through `update_status` when a Subcontracting Order is submitted, cancelled or changes status.
5. `erpnext/manufacturing/doctype/work_order/services/status.py::StatusService.update_planned_qty` passes only `planned_qty`. It is reached through `WorkOrder.update_planned_qty` when a Work Order is submitted, closed or cancelled. It returns early if `track_semi_finished_goods` is set.
6. `erpnext/accounts/services/child_item_update.py::update_bin_on_delete` passes `reserved_qty` for a Sales Order, or `ordered_qty` (plus `indented_qty` if the row has a material request item) otherwise. The call chain is `ChildItemUpdater.update` → `validate_and_delete_children` → `update_bin_on_delete`, which runs when you delete a row through "Update Items" on a submitted order.

**Caller that would keep working:**

`erpnext/stock/stock_balance.py::repost_stock` always builds a dict with all four keys from `get_reserved_qty`, `get_indented_qty`, `get_ordered_qty` and `get_planned_qty`. With `only_bin` it also adds `actual_qty`, which is an extra key and doesn't break the check. It is reached from `Item.after_rename` → `Item.recalculate_bin_qty` (renaming or merging an Item) and from `stock_balance.py::repost`. One caveat: with `only_actual=True` it never calls `update_bin_qty` at all.

`ProductionPlan.update_bin_qty` (`production_plan.py`, line 480) has the same name but is a different method. It calls `Bin.update_reserved_qty_for_production_plan`, not `stock_balance.update_bin_qty`, so the change doesn't affect it.
